      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Dizziness when standing up, known as orthostatic hypotension, can be a known side effect of lisinopril. However, **do not** increase your dosage without consulting your doctor first, as this could be dangerous. It is important to contact your healthcare provider to discuss these dizzy spells, as they can advise on whether an adjustment is needed or if other steps are appropriate.",
      "source": "target",
