      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Self-adjusting your medication dose, even just once, is not safe because it can unpredictably lower your blood pressure too much. The spinning feeling is a common sign that your body is adjusting to the new dosage, not necessarily that you need a stronger immediate dose. Please try to take your medication as prescribed and focus on moving slowly when changing positions until you can connect with your doctor.",
      "source": "target",
